metal2vulkan runtime: imported host pages in a type that is not coherent are flushed and invalidated too (Scion)

Upstream:  metal2vulkan, https://github.com/steelbrain/metal2vulkan, at 720ef1ce9ae2a2068999a8675717418b9416283e, after
           AdrenoMetal's 16 patches to it and Scion's 0001 to 0007; tools/metal/mk-metal2vulkan.sh applies them in that order,
           then this.
Licence:   GPL-2.0-or-later OR LGPL-3.0-or-later, metal2vulkan's (its LICENSE); this patch is a change to it and under the same
           terms. Nothing of it is in Scion's MIT or APSL files.
Author:    the HakiOS authors (Scion), 14 November 2026.

Why. PanVK on the Galaxy S9's Mali now imports a no-copy buffer's host pages (tools/mesa/panvk/panvk-host-surfaces.patch,
HakiosMali's request 0x7b), where metal2vulkan used to copy them in and out at every commit (0002). The window server on
Metal made 137 such buffers (build 55) and spent 78 ms a commit copying them in and 48 ms comparing them out. The pages are
the process's own cached memory, and the Mali does not see the processors' caches, so PanVK imports them into a memory
type that is HOST_VISIBLE | HOST_CACHED and not coherent, and cleans and invalidates their lines in
vkFlushMappedMemoryRanges and vkInvalidateMappedMemoryRanges. 0001 already takes those steps for a command buffer's
buffers in memory that is not coherent, but Buffer::host_span gave no span for a buffer over the caller's memory, so an
imported no-copy buffer was never flushed: the GPU would read what the CPU's caches had not yet written back.

What. Buffer::host_span gives a no-copy buffer's span in its import, whose placement is mapped at the caller's pointer
(as a heap's buffer over a no-copy heap's pages gets its heap's); only the memory of a caller's VkBuffer, which the runtime
does not map, still has none. host_sync::sync still flushes and invalidates only spans in memory that is not coherent, so
on a coherent import (every device before this, and an IOSurface's pages on PanVK) nothing changes.

--- a/crates/metal2vulkan-runtime/src/buffer.rs
+++ b/crates/metal2vulkan-runtime/src/buffer.rs
@@ -2000,11 +2000,16 @@
     /// Whose memory the buffer's bytes are, where they are the caller's: a no-copy buffer's
     /// host pages, or the memory of the caller's `VkBuffer`; a heap buffer's, its heap's (a heap
     /// over host pages, `Device::new_heap_with_bytes_no_copy`).
-    /// Where the bytes `contents` points at lie in the runtime's host-visible memory, for a flush
-    /// or an invalidate (`host_sync.rs`): `None` for `Private` storage and for memory the caller
-    /// made (host pages, a `VkBuffer`), which the runtime does not map.
+    /// Where the bytes `contents` points at lie in host-visible memory, for a flush or an
+    /// invalidate (`host_sync.rs`): the runtime's own, or the import of a no-copy buffer's host
+    /// pages, whose placement is mapped at the caller's pointer (Scion: a device that imports them
+    /// into a type that is not coherent, PanVK on the Mali, needs the steps there too); `None` for
+    /// `Private` storage and for the memory of a caller's `VkBuffer`, which the runtime does not
+    /// map.
     pub(super) fn host_span(&self) -> Option<crate::host_sync::HostSpan> {
-        if self.storage_mode() == StorageMode::Private || self.caller_memory().is_some() {
+        if self.storage_mode() == StorageMode::Private
+            || matches!(self.caller_memory(), Some(CallerMemory::VkBuffer))
+        {
             return None;
         }
         let span = |placement: &Placement, offset: u64, size: u64| {
